    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1e8f3bf74ac642f740d13a9c51682e94dceb791dc041cb773e8486535207efdd",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The appendices discharge two dependencies left open in the main construction. The generalized contour expansion's claimed containment of the earlier critical-line formula is justified by specializing parameters, cancelling gamma poles against trivial zeta zeros, reflecting the residual contour through the functional equation, and continuing the resulting identity. Separately, the gamma-ratio monotonicities used in the remainder estimate are supplied by product and integral representations, so representation compatibility and error control rest on distinct, explicit analytic mechanisms.",
