    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_3b5649c329dbb7b2e654639d9de2d59831141bd4be41ba631b33e0bee6636ec5",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a three-stage reliability chain: Mellin-contour displacement produces the smoothed expansion together with an explicit remainder, gamma-ratio monotonicity converts that contour remainder into a computable positive-tail certificate, and comparison with actual critical-line errors audits where the certificate is informative. The numerical expansion can remain highly accurate at truncations for which the available bound is already deteriorating, separating representation performance from certificate sharpness.",
